Package: bssd
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Safety Signal Detection for Blinded Clinical Trial Data
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Gosuke", "Homma", email = "gosuke.homma@astellas.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6854-5627"))
Description: Computes the posterior probability of a safety signal from
    blinded clinical trial data with the models of Duncan (2026)
    <doi:10.1080/10543406.2024.2395532>: the Poisson-based model of
    Mukhopadhyay, Waterhouse and Hartford (2018) <doi:10.1002/pst.1898> with
    the total exposure time or the total time at risk, the exponential
    Bernoulli mixture model, and the log-logistic Bernoulli mixture model.
    Other published methods for blinded data are included: the
    exposure-time Poisson model of Schnell and Ball (2016)
    <doi:10.1177/2168479016656702>, the binomial model of Ball and Schnell
    (2016) <doi:10.1007/978-3-319-42568-9_17>, the method of Gould and Wang
    (2017) <doi:10.1002/sim.7129>, the meta-analytic predictive prior and
    mixture likelihood of Brock et al. (2023) <doi:10.1002/pst.2278>, the
    meta-analysis of several blinded studies of Goren et al. (2020)
    <doi:10.1007/s43441-020-00183-7>, and the monitoring tools of Waterhouse
    et al. (2022) <doi:10.1002/pst.2175>. All posterior quantities are
    obtained by numerical integration instead of Markov chain Monte Carlo
    sampling. Functions to simulate blinded trial data, to estimate the
    operating characteristics of the models by simulation, and to compute
    decision boundaries for event counts and their exact operating
    characteristics are included.
